<span class="stamp">The Boardwalk</span>
<h1>Which Claw?</h1>
<p class="lede">The claw ecosystem has grown. Here's the lay of the land as of April 2026.</p>

<div class="claw-option">
  <h3>OpenClaw <span class="tag">main</span></h3>
  <p>The full-featured AI assistant runtime. Python-based, connects to Telegram, Discord, Signal, Slack, and more. Has plugins, skills, cron jobs, subagents, memory, and a growing ClawHub ecosystem. 211K+ GitHub stars since November 2025 (started as Clawdbot → Moltbot → OpenClaw).</p>
  <p class="stars"><span class="pulse"></span> 211K stars · 2026.4.14 latest (GPT-5.4 routing, security hardening, 138+ CVEs tracked)</p>
</div>

<div class="claw-option">
  <h3>NanoClaw <span class="tag">lightweight</span></h3>
  <p>A containerized, security-first alternative to OpenClaw. Runs in containers for isolation. Connects to WhatsApp, Telegram, Slack, Discord, Gmail, and other messaging apps. Has memory, scheduled jobs, and runs directly on Anthropic's Agents SDK.</p>
  <p>Latest preview includes Vercel Chat SDK integration (15 messaging platforms from one codebase) and one-tap approval dialogs for sensitive agent actions.</p>
  <p class="stars"><span class="pulse"></span> High velocity — 36-50 PRs per day tracked as of early April</p>
</div>

<div class="claw-option">
  <h3>PicoClaw <span class="tag">ultra-light</span></h3>
  <p>Written entirely in Go for sub-second startup and static binary distribution. A single native binary with no runtime dependencies — designed for ultra-portable hardware including $10-class devices and RISC-V boards.</p>
  <p>Built through a self-bootstrapping process where the AI agent itself drove the entire architectural migration and code optimization. Channel auto-orchestration and capability interfaces are live.</p>
  <p class="stars"><span class="pulse"></span> 20K+ stars in just 17 days · v0.2.6 released April 8</p>
</div>

<div class="claw-option">
  <h3>ZeroClaw <span class="tag">minimal</span></h3>
  <p>The most stripped-down variant — bare-bones AI agent runtime for minimal environments. Targets edge cases where even PicoClaw might be overkill.</p>
</div>

<div class="claw-option">
  <h3>NemoClaw <span class="tag">enterprise</span></h3>
  <p>NVIDIA's enterprise wrapper for OpenClaw — sandboxed, guarded, managed. Runs OpenClaw inside NVIDIA OpenShell with Landlock + seccomp + network namespace isolation. Policy-based guardrails for every network request, file access, and inference call.</p>
  <p>Launched March 16 at GTC 2026. Still in early preview — interfaces may change without notice. Showcased at National Robotics Week for translating text instructions into physical robot actions via Isaac Sim.</p>
</div>

<h2>How to choose</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Want everything?</strong> Go with <a href="/">OpenClaw</a>. It's the main event.</li>
  <li><strong>Need container security?</strong> <a href="#nanoclaw">NanoClaw</a> is your friend.</li>
  <li><strong>Running on a microcontroller or $10 board?</strong> <a href="#picoclaw">PicoClaw</a> (Go binary, no deps).</li>
  <li><strong>Enterprise deployment?</strong> <a href="/nemoclaw/">NemoClaw</a> wraps OpenClaw for production.</li>
  <li><strong>Minimal, bare-bones?</strong> <a href="#zeroclaw">ZeroClaw</a> exists for the edge cases.</li>
</ul>

